WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.560
Fans of the famous Dude Perfect group will&nbsp;
surely be familiar with the two twins, Coby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.760
and Cory Cotton, also known as Twin #1 and Twin&nbsp;
#2, respectively. It's hard to keep up with them;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.120
although they are identical twins,&nbsp;
the two of them lead different lives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:16.560
While both brothers are a part of the crazy&nbsp;
trick shot crew, one of them is a published&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.200
author with a wife and kids. The other has&nbsp;
lost the most battles in Dude Perfect history.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.560
Younger brother Cory Cotton can lay&nbsp;
claim to having the most wins, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.880
there's a lot you probably don't know about him.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.000
One of the first things you will notice&nbsp;
about Cory when you start to dig deeper into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.200
his life is his real first name&nbsp;
is not Cory. Born July 17, 1987,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.680
Cory Cotton was born William Cory Cotton,&nbsp;
according to the Dude Perfect Fandom site.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.440
This is also the case for his twin brother,&nbsp;
Coby, who was born John Coby Cotton.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.520
Of course, it doesn't exactly help keep things&nbsp;
simple when two twins with similar names like Cory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:53.200
and Coby become friends with a guy named Cody, as&nbsp;
in Cody Jones. Fortunately it's easy for fans to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.840
tell the three men apart, as the twins are easily&nbsp;
distinguishable based on physical characteristics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.720
and Cody looks nothing like them at all.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:05.680
Speaking of twins, they tend to run in the Cotton&nbsp;
family. Cory Cotton is already known as Twin #2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.120
born only a minute behind his twin&nbsp;
brother, Coby, who's known as Twin #1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:13.120
This twin-sibling rivalry is one of the&nbsp;
best dynamics seen throughout the various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.720
Dude Perfect media, and Cory seems&nbsp;
to better his brother in that aspect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.120
Cory has won a total of seven battles,&nbsp;
while his older brother has only won four.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:24.960
And it doesn't look like the twin-sibling&nbsp;
rivalry will stop with Cory and Coby.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.760
On November 18, 2018, Cory and his wife,&nbsp;
Amy Surplus, became parents to twins and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:33.680
named them Crew and Collins. They're&nbsp;
probably too young for a fierce sibling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.760
rivalry like the one between their dad and&nbsp;
uncle, but it will likely happen one day.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:42.320
Most of the guys in Dude Perfect have some sort&nbsp;
of role outside of making incredible trick shots.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.320
According to Fandom, Cory likes to help the&nbsp;
editing team make the final version of the video.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.640
This may not seem to be within his particular&nbsp;
wheelhouse — Cory received a Bachelor of Arts in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.360
Speech Communications from Texas A&amp;M University,&nbsp;
according to his LinkedIn profile — but when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.200
an extra hand was needed for the editing&nbsp;
process, Cory was the first to jump in.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.320
Coby, also a communications&nbsp;
major, helps with the mobile apps.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:06.320
The Dude Perfect guys have had to face some&nbsp;
hilarious and sometimes cruel punishments over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:11.520
the years; Unfortunately for Cory, he received&nbsp;
probably one of the worst punishments ever.

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.920
"Just, I have had a bad streak."
In Overtime 7, Cory had to shave his eyebrows.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:21.120
Eyebrows don't grow back overnight; it takes&nbsp;
about 4-16 weeks for eyebrows to grow back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.840
This is hands-down the longest lasting punishment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.960
making it probably one of the&nbsp;
worst ones fans have ever seen.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.480
Cory doesn't only make trick-shot videos&nbsp;
and suffer through entertaining punishments&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.760
for a living. In 2011, Cory published Go Big:&nbsp;
Make Your Shot Count in the Connected World.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.040
This book took readers behind the&nbsp;
scenes of Dude Perfect and dove deep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.240
into the "Go Big" philosophy. The&nbsp;
book also goes into their secrets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.840
of success and shares some tips on how&nbsp;
to take your passion to the next level.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.040
It's just one of the many things the&nbsp;
guys from Dude Perfect have accomplished,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:53.760
aside from the YouTube series, documentary, mobile&nbsp;
apps, and tours. Most of the guys have admitted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.920
they don't want to make trick-shot videos forever.&nbsp;
Although they would like to keep the brand alive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.480
they realize they will have to focus on other&nbsp;
things, such as family and other career ventures.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:07.600
For Cory, he has his three children and wife to&nbsp;
focus on, and possibly more books in the future.

